*Operator Algebra:* The commutator of a product of operators is given by the identity $[A B, C] = A[B, C] + [A, C]B$. The adjoint operator $a^dagger$ and the annihilation operator $a$ satisfy the canonical commutation relation $[a, a^dagger] = 1$.
